{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For a fire has kindled in My anger.</b> For I had chastised them so that they would return. <b>And it burns to the lowest Sheol.</b> They added transgression to their sin, in that they provoked My wrath until I brought them down to the lowest Sheol — as in the case of Ahaz, as it says: וּבְעֵת הָצֵר לוֹ וַיּוֹסֶף לִמְעוֹל בַה׳ (II Chronicles 28:22)." "<b>And it consumes the foundations of the mountains.</b> He removed from them all the leaders of the people, as it says: מֵסִיר מִירוּשָׁלַיִם וּמִיהוּדָה מַשְׁעֵן וּמַשְׁעֵנָה גִּבּוֹר וְאִישׁ מִלְחָמָה יוֹעֵץ וְנָבִיא כוּ׳ (Isaiah 3:1–3)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:09.600966992Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}